cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this research concept and its specific Git commit. The publication includes a measurement architecture, implementation path and supporting numerical studies."
title: "FacetCensus: Display-Integrated Optical Sensing for Scene Geometry and Surface Appearance"
authors:
  - family-names: Dik
    given-names: Philipp
version: "2026.09.29"
date-released: "2026-09-29"
url: "https://github.com/PhilDik/Perceptive-Pixel"
abstract: >-
  Research concept for environment geometry and surface appearance estimation
  from calibrated display-associated optical measurements, illumination states
  and registered panel motion. Planar receivers and multi-region pixels are
  candidate implementations. Includes a prior-work review and limited numerical
  examples with their assumptions, plus an available-component planning calculation.
keywords:
  - display-integrated sensing
  - computational imaging
  - scene reconstruction
  - surface appearance
  - research concept
